    "body": "The added note seems accurate and adds a useful clarification. I think some details could be omitted, the important point is that \"foreign content\" is not an insertion mode and functions independently.\n\nIt seems most useful around [the section that describes the insertion mode.](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#insertion-mode)\n\n---\n\nI just spotted a related line that needs to be changed, refers to foreign content as an insertion mode [(13.2.5.69 CDATA section state)](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#cdata-section-state):\n\n> U+0000 NULL characters are handled in the tree construction stage, as part of the in foreign content insertion mode, which is the only place where CDATA sections can appear. \n\n",
